Privacy Policy

Privacy Policy for Stencil AI

Last Updated: June 30, 2025

Welcome to Stencil AI ("we," "us," or "our"). We are committed to protecting your privacy. This Privacy Policy explains how we collect, use, disclose, and safeguard your information when you use our application.

By using our service, you agree to the collection and use of information in accordance with this policy.

1. Information We Collect

Based on your use of our service, we may collect the following types of information:

    Account Information: When you create an account, we collect your name, email address, and a password digest (your password is encrypted and we cannot see it).

    User-Generated Content:

        Prompts and Conversations: We store the messages (your prompts and the AI responses), conversations, and artifacts (the outputs you generate, including Mermaid diagrams) that you create.

        Custom Prompts ("Artifact Stencils"): We store the custom prompt artifact stencils that you create, including the name, prompt, and description.

    Usage Data:

        We automatically collect information about your session, including your IP address and user agent to ensure the security of your account.

        We log your usage of the AI models through OpenRouter, including the model used, token counts, and associated cost. This is to manage our service and prepare for future billing.

    Cookies: We use essential cookies for session management to keep you logged in. We do not currently use cookies for analytics or tracking, but we may in the future. We will update this policy if that changes.

2. How We Use Your Information

We use the information we collect to:

    Provide, operate, and maintain our service.

    Manage your account and your projects.

    Allow you to create, save, and manage your conversations and artifacts.

    Monitor the usage of our service for performance and cost management.

    Prepare for the introduction of different account tiers.

    Improve the user experience.

3. Data Sharing and Third-Party Sub-processors

To provide our core AI functionality, we must share some of your data with third-party services (known as "sub-processors").

    AI Model Providers: When you generate content, we send your messages and the relevant context to third-party AI model providers through an intermediary API service (currently OpenRouter). These providers process your prompts and return the generated content (text, diagrams, etc.).

        We do not send personally identifiable information like your email address or name with these requests.

        The specific AI models we use may change over time based on performance, cost, and features. We will always choose reputable providers with strong privacy standards.

        These underlying AI services have their own privacy policies. By using our Service, you acknowledge that your User Content will be processed by these third parties as necessary to provide the functionality.

    Future Analytics: We may in the future use services like Google Analytics, Sentry, or Honeybadger to monitor application performance and user engagement. We will update this policy if and when we add these services.

4. Data Storage and Security

    Your data is stored on PostgreSQL databases hosted on Hetzner servers located in Germany.

    While we take data security seriously, please note that your chat content is not encrypted at rest in our database. As the administrator, I have access to this data to maintain the service. We ask that you do not input sensitive personal or financial information into the chat.

5. Data Retention and Your Rights

You have control over your data:

    Account Deletion: You can delete your account at any time. When you delete your account, all your associated data, including projects, conversations, and artifacts, will be permanently deleted from our database.

    Access and Correction: You have the right to access and update your account information at any time.

    GDPR and PIPEDA Rights: If you are a resident of the European Economic Area (EEA) or Canada, you have certain data protection rights. These include the right to access, update, or delete your information.

6. Age Requirement

Users must be 18 years of age or older to use our service. This is due to the potential for the AI to generate content that is not suitable for minors and because we plan to offer paid features.

7. Changes to This Privacy Policy

We may update our Privacy Policy from time to time. We will notify you of any changes by posting the new Privacy Policy on this page.

8. Contact Us

If you have any questions about this Privacy Policy, please contact us at support@stencil-ai.xyz.